## Side note: macOS / Apple Silicon
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Does not build as-is (CL/cl.h vs OpenCL/cl.h include path; no __APPLE__
branch in getExecutableDir). With those two host fixes it compiles and lists
the GPU, but every filter fails at clCreateKernel with "newComputePipelineState
failed" because Apple's OpenCL-on-Metal has no fp64 and the kernel is
double throughout. Apple's OpenCL front end does accept the source, so a Mac
is usable as a syntax checker for kernel edits, not as a runner.

