## Change applied (2026-09-03) — fp64 divide removed from pseudohash (lib/util.cl)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Measured before this change, 16 groups/CU, roundDigits already divide-free:
erratic_flush_five 500M seeds 3.00 s (was 3.5 s before the roundDigits
change: -14%).

pseudohash's per-character 1.1239285023/num was the last fp64 divide on the
hot path: 8 per seed in i_new plus one per character of each new node's
name, all serially dependent. The divisor varies, so unlike div_1e13 the
reciprocal is refined at run time: float reciprocal seed (~24 bits), two
Newton steps (e0 = fma(-b,r,1); y1 = fma(e0,r,r); y2 = fma(e0*e0,y1,y1)),
then the Markstein residual step (q = a*y2; rr = fma(-b,q,a); fma(rr,y2,q)).
Correctly rounded fp64 `/` and fma() are mandated by OpenCL, so the result is
bit-identical to a/b. Falls back to `/` for b < 1e-37, which cannot occur
for a fract() output in practice.

Host validation against `/`: 3e8 divisors (half uniform in (0,1], half
log-uniform down to 1e-30), 2e7 random strings of 1..30 chars over a wide
alphabet, 3e6 seed strings, and 1e7 node-name strings (e.g. "erratic" or
"Joker1sho1" followed by 8 seed chars), each also with the float seed
perturbed by -4..+4 ulp to model an approximate native reciprocal: zero
mismatches in every set.

Side note found while validating: the kernel's `(1<<k)` with k = 32 is a
shift by the operand width, which C and OpenCL C leave undefined. NVIDIA
lowers it as a masked shift, giving 1, so on that driver the int_part /
fract_part elaboration is a no-op scale by 1. It was left exactly as written
since changing it would change output on any driver that behaves otherwise.

Windows golden run still required; perkeo_observatory is the important
filter here since it hashes many distinct node names per seed.

Independent verification (read-only, second model family): no behaviour-
changing defect. Confirmed the two Newton steps leave the reciprocal within
~1 ulp (error ~delta^4 from a <= 2^-22 seed, then fp64 rounding dominates),
which satisfies the Markstein / Cornea-Harrison-Tang precondition for the
residual step to be correctly rounded; re-ran 3e8 random and 3e8 adversarial
(rounding-boundary) divisors with perturbed seeds, zero mismatches; confirmed
num == 0 gives +inf on both old and new paths; confirmed the host passes no
fast-math or mad-enable build options. Two comment inaccuracies fixed.
